cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it as below, and cite the underlying data archives listed in docs/DATA_SOURCES.md."
title: "Finding Earth 2.0: From the Observed Exoplanet Catalogue to Selection-Corrected Temperate Terrestrial Planet Inference"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jana"
    given-names: "Biswajit"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Biswajit1999/finding-earth-2"
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
abstract: >
  A reproducible evidence architecture connecting the observed exoplanet
  catalogue to selection-corrected population inference, composition-model
  disagreement, time-dependent climate context, stellar environment,
  atmospheric observability, direct-imaging scenarios, information gain, and
  Solar-System falsification controls. It makes no claim of life detection.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - astrobiology
  - habitable zone
  - computational astrophysics
  - reproducible research
  - selection effects
  - Bayesian inference
  - direct imaging
